  "body": "## Finite bit construction \u2014 no new kappa\n\nSeven fully paid **ordered, overlapping helper shears** improve the historical PR543 R420 nine-total decoder beyond PR708's frozen disjoint matching: **321 \u2192 250 decoder XORs** including preparation/restoration, and **26,916 \u2192 26,774 complete native ADDs** after rebuilding literal reverse cleanup. This saves 142 against the original and 28 beyond PR708. The circuit contains **six noncommuting shear pairs**; wrong-order restoration and wrong-order covector substitution are both explicitly rejected.\n\nOnly `research/r420-decoder-chain/` is added. D, scatter, B, the complete arbitrary-dirt A operator, all 660 register-frame paths, original H1\u2013H5, helpers/copies and paid profile `{1:1320,2:1440,4:60,5:120,8:9}` remain unchanged. No selected supplier or frontier change.\n\n### Exact reproducibility and evidence\n\nBase: `1b59b624d21924f8e3537cdc1ac52d3be6eda2fe`.\nAssignment: OS seed **07**, bit-supplier track. The local claim records three candidates and the absence of a pinned coordination issue.\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/r420-decoder-chain/verify.py\n```\n\nExpected final line:\n\n```text\nPASS_R420_DECODER_CHAIN decoder=321->250 ADDs=26916->26774 columns=660 controls=8 noncommuting=6 no_new_kappa\n```\n\n- Source-bound certificate regeneration, unchanged exact E8/frame/interface checker, separate set-valued complete-word interpreter and **eight negative controls** pass.\n- Bounded search: all **6,320 directed pairs** at each of **seven steps**, 44,240 scores total; deterministic seed7 ties. No restarts; stopping at seven is **not an optimum claim**.\n- Fresh unchanged C++ legality and full **nine-stage native replay for both words**, **1,380 formal columns and 18/18 omitted-bridge controls each**, pass.\n- Native payload rises **100 \u2192 103 bits**, still strictly below 104. Candidate forward/reverse positive bounds are **219,001 / 2,932,970**; exact payload upper `5782737910556506080751636537600`. No inherited precision charge is silently reused.\n- Exact sources, canonical word hashes, ordered recipe, per-step coverage, proof, native receipt and commands are committed. The environment lacked C++; a user-local GCC15 C++ frontend plus existing Boost resolved the prerequisite without changing checks. Failed prerequisite attempts are disclosed.\n\n### Novelty and credit\n\nThis reuses and credits eumemic's **PR543** construction/checker and Sagar Thakrar's **PR708** recipe, independent interpreter and native replay design. **PR753** already improves disjoint pairs to disjoint restored stars (decoder257); this result changes the class to ordered noncommuting chains and reaches250, without claiming global optimality. **PR748** achieves larger overall savings by changing the helper-dirt map and D; this work preserves both and claims no overall record. **PR848**'s selected-R439 disjoint-total obstruction is respected: this construction is historical R420 only.\n\nDylan Crow, DreamingOfClouds, Zhihao Chen and the retained realization/hosting/assembly lineage remain credited. Prepared by **Adam Gall (@adamgall)** with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance**, Apache-2.0, preserving predecessor licenses and notices. No independent human review is claimed.\n\n### Scope limits\n\nThe accepted result at this base remains PR1042, conditional \u03ba `0.001672188119205421`, with PR589-on-PR555 bit supplier. Scalar savings do not improve the recursive moment. Full hosted-parent/global invoice, selected cold replay, outer assembly, repository-wide suite, Lean and remote CI were not run; none are claimed. Inherited all-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-basis realization, whole-call hosting, residual, precision/tape and analytic assumptions remain. This is finite circuit evidence, not a full multiplication proof.\n",
